WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.750 align:start position:0%
 
we'll start with the lowest hanging  fruit which relates to the decision that  came last night from le'veon bell  reportedly choosing between the bills  the chiefs and the dolphins and then he  narrowed it to the chiefs and the  dolphins and frankly in all due respect  to the dolphins  if you're gonna narrow it to those two  teams  you're gonna take the chiefs you're  gonna you're gonna ride with the  champions you're gonna go with the  opportunity to play deep into january  pump up your resume and hit the market  next year because it's a one-year deal  as everyone expected it to be it allows  him to become a free agent after the  season and  this is a a win-win right if bell still  has it peter this is a win-win for him  and for a team that could use a  compliment to rookie clyde edwards  well the reason why this pairing works  so well is that andy reed wants to throw  the ball to the running backs out of the  backfield he wants to design plays  for these great wheel routes  uh you saw what he did with kareem hunt  right away in 2017 in new england he  designed a play with  kareem hunt on dante hightower and it  went for 70 plus yards and a touchdown  that is what andy reid loves to do he  loves to not only have his receivers to  be threats in the intermediate part of  the field but also his running backs  that's where i think le'veon bell was  swayed and that's why the chiefs really  wanted him i'm sure the money is not  that much  for kansas city and you know i also  think everybody was  really excited about clyde edwards  hilaire at the beginning of the year and  rightfully so  he's an excellent player and i think  he's going to have a great career  but  when you  focus so much on one player in one  running back and yeah they they have  other backs in their stable  but  you know le'veon bell is going to give  them the opportunity to have a we think  but we don't know a premiere back out of  the backfield mike the reason why we  don't know  is that le'veon bell sat out 2018  he was mediocre the last year and a  third  uh with the jets so i mean think about  it mike it's been three years  since le'veon bell has been great  so is he still great he'll tell you he  is  the chiefs will tell you we think he is  but we simply do not know we just don't  know  yeah and you look at how it tails off on  the chart from the football perspective  twitter account the the gold dots with  the black rim are his performances with  the steelers and then the cluster at the  right where it all drops off that's what  happened with the jets now last year he  still had  a decent season by running back  standards 1200 plus yards from scrimmage  but it wasn't le'veon bell standards it  wasn't 13.5 million a year with the  first two years and 27 million  guaranteed let me spin back to clyde  edwards elaire because when they drafted  him  the thought was this year it would be  damian williams and clyde edward zelaire  sharing the load that's what brett veach  the gm of the team told me just days  after the draft this isn't we're making  clyde edwards elaire the number one guy  and damien just gets pushed aside damian  williams played really well in the super  bowl and helped contribute significantly  to the victory but then williams opts  out over the pandemic  and we all just kind of say oh well it's  clyde edwards well you know what they  made a play for adrian peterson which  tells you they've been thinking about  this  for a while and last year they made a  play for le'veon bell when the jets were  talking to teams about trading and bell  said so it was the packers it was the  chiefs it was the texans it was the  steelers and there was one more that i  keep forgetting but there were teams  that were interested in him last year he  just wasn't interested  in revising the contract that paid him  27 million fully guaranteed and you look  at edwards elaire's performance he blew  us away with 138 yards rushing in week  one since then 70 total yards from  scrimmage against the chargers 64 yards  rushing against the ravens he added 70  receiving so that had him at 134 from  scrimmage he had 91 yards from scrimmage  in the win over the patriots and then  most recently 40 yards rushing 40 yards  receiving so he has not been tearing it  up the way that maybe we thought he was  going to right out of the gates and they  could use the help and a great point  chris made yesterday when we were  talking about what le'veon bell can do  if you put him in the backfield and you  run the ball and run the ball and run  the ball  that is going to get the defense to  react and maybe they sneak another  linebacker on the field to stop him as a  runner well once you get them in that  matchup you split him to the slot and  you let him go 70 yards against that  linebacker for a touchdown and that's  where le'veon bell becomes that mismatch  if you react to what he can do as a  running back he'll kill you as a  receiver  yeah and i think look no one's  criticizing clyde edwards hilaire he's  on pace for a  whatever almost 1100 yard rushing season  you know that's good  but i think  you know  i remember when i left kansas city camp  in august  i just told everybody take clyde edward  solaire  you know as you're running back and  again look if you took them over  christian mccaffrey and saquon barkley  you're a genius  but  i in in general in general  i really did think especially in the  running game he was going to have given  the chiefs more  and especially after the first game of  the season but look this is classic andy  reid you know what he does  he basically overloads his stable  because he knows he understands that in  week 11  clyde edwards hilaire is going to get a  turf toe or a you know a strained calf  or something like that you know very  very rarely do your finely tuned  athletes  uh like edward hilaire is very rarely do  they  go through a 16 game regular season  without something happening to make them  less than a hundred percent and look  you know what  you know the one thing that le'veon bell  has done in the last year and a half is  pretty much conserve himself you know he  he's not had a heavy workload so to me  this just this is absolutely what andy  reid does every single year it's like a  a reed belichick move let's take  an undervalued penny stock  and let's let's let him grow  you know in our portfolio and that's  what i think le'veon bell is going to do  and they tried that last year with  lesean mccoy when he fell into the  chief's lap he was cut labor day weekend  by the bills somewhat surprisingly mccoy  really didn't do all that much and by  the time we got to the end of the season  he wasn't even active for some of the  most important postseason games so we'll  see what le'veon bell has the chiefs  will find out what le'veon bell has but  what he definitely has is a team that  wants him and it was never really all  that clear that the jets wanted him mike  mckagne did he paid too much adam gase  knew he paid too much mcagne frankly got  grifted by someone in bell's camp that  made  mccagnan believe the ravens were at the  table for the same amount and they never  were and it never got that relationship  off to a good start so no longer a jet  now a chief november 1 he gets to play  the jets who handed  le'veon bell to the open market and he  lands in kansas city  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

